(: One record by identifier, for GetRecord. Returns nothing if absent, so
   the caller can raise idDoesNotExist. A tombstone yields the header with no
   payload - GetRecord for a deleted record must not invent metadata.

   The identifier is globally unique because each module tags its records with
   its own prefix (object-, person-, asset-), so a search across all
   sources finds exactly one - the caller need not know which database holds it.

   Same split as paging: SOURCE gives the header, PAYLOADS attaches the payload
   for the record asked for. A derived format (oai_dc) is built there too, so it
   is assembled for the record actually served.

   (Placeholders are plain words here on purpose - the renderer substitutes every
   double-brace placeholder, comments included.)
:)
{{NAMESPACES}}
{{FORMAT_NAMESPACES}}
{{OAI_DATE_FUNCTION}}
{{ZETCOM_FUNCTION}}

declare variable $db external;
(: absolute path to vocmap.xml, for the related-works ISIL lookup. An unbound
   external variable is an error, so it is always bound even when unused. :)
declare variable $vocmap external;
declare variable $tzOffset external;
declare variable $identifier external;
declare variable $withPayload external;

let $rows := {{SOURCE}}
let $wanted := $rows[@identifier = $identifier]
let $payloads := if ($withPayload = 'true') then {{PAYLOADS}} else ()

return
  for $r in $wanted
  return
    <row datestamp="{$r/@datestamp}"
         identifier="{$r/@identifier}"
         status="{$r/@status}"
         sets="{$r/@sets}">{
      $payloads[@id = $r/@identifier]/node()
    }</row>
